enter"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The 40-bed Upper Shore Community Mental Health Center, a psychiatric hospital that was located in Chestertown, and the Eastern Shore Hospital Center were jointly administered for a number of years.","title":"Eastern Shore Hospital Center"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The Upper Shore Community Mental Health Center was closed in March 2010.","title":"Eastern Shore Hospital Center"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"A hospital is a health care institution providing patient treatment with specialized medical and nursing staff and medical equipment.","title":"Hospital"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The best-known type of hospital is the general hospital, which typically has an emergency department to treat urgent health problems ranging from fire and accident victims to a heart attack.","title":"Hospital"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" A district hospital typically is the major health care facility in its region, with large numbers of beds for intensive care and additional beds for patients who need long-term care.","title":"Hospital"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Specialised hospitals include trauma centres, rehabilitation hospitals, children's hospitals, seniors' (geriatric) hospitals, and hospitals for dealing with specific medical needs such as psychiatric treatment (see psychiatric hospital) and certain disease categories.","title":"Hospital"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Specialised hospitals can help reduce health care costs compared to general hospitals.","title":"Hospital"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"A state hospital is a hospital funded and operated by the government of a state.","title":"State hospital"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" In some countries, such as South Africa, the term is synonymous with public hospital.","title":"State hospital"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" In other countries, like the United States, general public hospitals are operated by local governments.","title":"State hospital"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Due in part to the efforts of Do