{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Chinese legend has it that the money tree (搖錢樹) is a kind of holy tree, which can bring money and fortune to the people, and that it is a symbol of affluence, nobility and auspiciousness.","title":"Money tree (myth)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It can be traced back to primitive societies when the adoration of a holy tree was prevalent.","title":"Money tree (myth)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Whilst Money trees may be derived from the Sun tree myth associated with paradise, the coins link paradise with a material bounty in this world.","title":"Money tree (myth)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" There also exists a holy tree named Chinese Hibiscus in Chinese mythology.","title":"Money tree (myth)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" According to the existing historical narratives, the concept of the "money tree" is derived at the latest from the Han Dynasty.","title":"Money tree (myth)"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Cast-bronze money trees are a conspicuous feature of Han tombs in Sichuan.","title":"Money tree (myth)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":""Money Trees Deuce" is a song by American hip hop recording artist Jay Rock, released as the first single from his second studio album, "90059".","title":"Money Trees Deuce"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The song, produced by Flippa and J Proof, is a follow-up to Kendrick Lamar's 2012 song, "Money Trees".","title":"Money Trees Deuce"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":""Money Trees" is a song by American hip hop recording artist Kendrick Lamar, taken from his major label debut studio album "Good Kid, M.A.A.D City" (2012).","title":"Money Trees"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The song, which appears as the fifth track on the album, features a guest appearance from his Black Hippy cohort, fellow American rapper Jay Rock.","title":"Money Trees"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The song, produced by DJ Dahi, entered the "Billboard" Bubbling Under Hot 100 chart at number 19 due to high downloads, following the album's release.","title":