{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Cynthia Ann Stephanie "Cyndi" Lauper (born June 22, 1953) is an American singer, songwriter, actress and LGBT rights activist.","title":"Cyndi Lauper"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Her career has spanned over 30 years.","title":"Cyndi Lauper"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Her debut solo album "She's So Unusual" (1983) was the first debut female album to chart four top-five hits on the "Billboard" Hot 100—"Girls Just Want to Have Fun", "Time After Time", "She Bop", and "All Through the Night"—and earned Lauper the Best New Artist award at the 27th Grammy Awards in 1985.","title":"Cyndi Lauper"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Her success continued with the soundtrack for the motion picture "The Goonies" and her second record "True Colors" (1986).","title":"Cyndi Lauper"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" This album included the number one single "True Colors" and "Change of Heart", which peaked at number 3.","title":"Cyndi Lauper"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The True Colors World Tour was a concert tour by American recording artist Cyndi Lauper.","title":"True Colors World Tour"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was Lauper's first headlining world tour in 1986-87 in support of her album, "True Colors".","title":"True Colors World Tour"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The True Colors tour included dates across North America, Asia and Europe.","title":"True Colors World Tour"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Ras Kimono is a Nigerian reggae artist whose debut album Under Pressure led by the single "Rum-Bar Stylée" was a big hit in the Nigerian music scene in 1989.","title":"Ras Kimono"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Before he released his solo album, he was in a group called "The Jastix" along with Amos McRoy and Majek Fashek.","title":"Ras Kimono"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"American singer Beyoncé has embarked on six concert tours during her solo career, four of which have been worldwide and two of which have been collaborative.","title":"List of Beyoncé live performances"}