ce abilities and the more advanced production seen compared to her previous tours.","title":"List of Beyoncé live performances"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"American singer Demi Lovato has embarked six concert tours and performed live at various award ceremonies and television shows.","title":"List of Demi Lovato live performances"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Her debut promotional tour in 2008, Demi Live!","title":"List of Demi Lovato live performances"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Warm Up Tour was based in North America only and supported her debut studio album, "Don't Forget" (2008).","title":"List of Demi Lovato live performances"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" At the same year, Lovato served as one of the opening acts for Jonas Brothers on their fifth concert tour, Burnin' Up Tour.","title":"List of Demi Lovato live performances"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Lovato also served as one of the opening acts for Avril Lavigne on her third concert tour, The Best Damn World Tour on selected dates in North America.","title":"List of Demi Lovato live performances"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" In 2009, Lovato performed as the opening act on the Jonas Brothers World Tour 2009 with Jonas Brothers during the South American and European legs, before she continued to tour her first headlining tour, during Summer 2009, promoting her debut album "Don't Forget" and her sophomore album "Here We Go Again".","title":"List of Demi Lovato live performances"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" The tour featured opening acts, David Archuleta, Jordan Pruitt and KSM.","title":"List of Demi Lovato live performances"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" In 2010, Lovato performed as the opening act on Jonas Brothers' Live in Concert World Tour 2010.","title":"List of Demi Lovato live performances"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" On November 1, 2010, Lovato left the tour after a dispute arose to the public light involving her apparently punching one of the dancers of the tour.","title":"List of Demi Lovato live performances"},{"s